docs: design draft for a read-only SHOP3 adapter over TMDM objects

A design note only: no adapter, no planning infrastructure and no code
are added. It describes how a client such as HyperDoc could export SHOP3
state atoms from a native topic-map through the public readers, keeping
three layers apart: the TMDM items as they are, the relationships
recognized by the TMDM 7.2/7.3 readers, and facts derived by named rules.
The warrant belongs to the fact record in the adapter, never to the TMDM
model. It lists the prerequisites still missing for a plan over real TMDM
objects and proposes the smallest next integration task.

The adapter would live in the client, not in this library; the note is
kept here because the library is where the readers it relies on are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
